course: dictionary
lesson: 8826
title: Place names and special words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Shetland is a place name, so it starts with a capital letter, just like London or Glasgow. Context can show you what kind of word it is. «Ponies are small horses... often from cold hilly places like Shetland, Wales or Dartmoor» tells you Shetland is a place, because it is in a list with Wales and Dartmoor.
explain: The same word can work in different ways. In «a Shetland pony», the word Shetland describes the pony, like a type of pony. In «the Shetland Islands», it names a place. Look at the words around it to see which job it is doing.
explain: «For its size a Shetland pony is one of the strongest horses and once pulled carts in coal mines.» Small and strong both fit, so the clues are the words for size and strength. Try your meaning in the sentence: a small, strong pony makes sense here, so you have understood it.
fact: Shetland is a group of islands in the far north of Scotland, between mainland Scotland and Norway.
fact: A Shetland pony is a very small, strong, hairy pony first bred in Shetland.
fact: Shetland wool is fine, soft wool from Shetland sheep, used to knit jumpers and shawls.
fact: Shetland is a place name, so it always has a capital letter.
fact: «Shetland ponies from cold Scottish islands grow thick winter coats» shows how the cold weather affects them.
exercise: In «Shetland is a group of islands in the far north of Scotland», what kind of word is Shetland? | A colour | *A place name, so it has a capital letter | A kind of wool | A sort of pony
exercise: In «a Shetland pony», what does Shetland tell you? | It is the name of a farm | It is a colour of the pony's coat | *It tells you which kind of pony it is, a small hardy breed
exercise: Copy the word that is a place name in «Ponies are often from cold hilly places like Shetland, Wales or Dartmoor». | hilly | ponies | cold | *Shetland
test: Which of these is true of a Shetland pony? | It lives in the desert | It is a kind of fishing boat | Its name means a fast racehorse | *It is a very small, strong, hairy pony first bred in Shetland
test: In «Shetland wool is used to knit jumpers and shawls», what is the wool used for? | Feeding ponies | Building boats | *Knitting jumpers and shawls | Lighting fires
exam: Which sentence uses Shetland as a place name? | «A Shetland pony is small and strong.» | «The Shetland wool was soft.» | *«We sailed north to the Shetland Islands.» | «She knitted a warm Shetland jumper.»
